WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
Or sit here and make up the words


00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.600
As we go along


00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:09.759
They told me maybe she's crazy


00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.159
A little like you


00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.160
Everyone said you were nothing but trouble


00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
And all that I know
is that I've never been here before


00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:25.040
I don't need to pretend anymore


00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.479
Strange, so strange


00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.759
You are hilarious.


00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:39.760
When it feels better being alone


00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.760
You'll accept there is nobody else


00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:46.599
Then set it in stone


00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:51.679
And they told me maybe she's crazy


00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:53.439
A little like you


00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.440
Everyone said...


00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:04.720
Will and I were just updating our band's
MySpace page.


00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.800
You know that kid, Will Burton?
Do some recon.


00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:18.119
Find out everything you can about him.


00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.120
They'll have his records in the office.
Where he's from, where he went to school.


00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.319
His guidance counsellor report,
that'll have all the good stuff. All right?


00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.919
Everything. And do it today.


00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:28.759
Whoa. Yo, dude,
we don't actually work for you.


00:01:28.760 --> 00:01:31.760
It's not like you're the Joker
and we're your henchmen.


00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.000
Fine. I'll do it myself.


00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:40.480
All right, best for last. Sa5m, Will?
Tell us who you are.


00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.560
My project is Will Burton.


00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:57.640
I'm pointing
because it's hard to tell who he is.


00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:02.520
I was going to use photographs
for this presentation,


00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:06.040
but then I realized, the real Will Burton
can't be captured on film.


00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.279
Instead,


00:02:12.280 --> 00:02:14.919
you need this.


00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:17.920
Will is a reflective surface.


00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:21.320
He mirrors back at you
whatever you want to see.


00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.680
He reflects you back to you.


00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.760
And it's nice for awhile.


00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.679
You stop feeling lonely.


00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.680
But then you realize,
he's doing that with everyone.


00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:41.520
The only person he can't do it for


00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.039
is Will.


00:02:44.040 --> 00:02:47.040
Because he doesn't have a clue


00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:50.120
who he is.


00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.679
Okay, well, that was very creative.


00:03:02.680 --> 00:03:05.680
And really mean. Okay, Will, you're up.


00:04:00.800 --> 00:04:03.800
If I told you things I did before


00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:07.160
Told you how I used to be


00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:10.440
Would you go along with someone like me?


00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:16.920
If you knew my story word for word


00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:20.560
Had all of my history


00:04:20.840 --> 00:04:23.840
Would you go along with someone like me?


00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:29.280
And we don't care about the young folks


00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.879
Talking about the young style


00:04:32.880 --> 00:04:35.879
And we don't care about the old folks


00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.880
Talking about the old style too


00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:42.560
And we don't care about our own faults


00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:46.239
Talking about our own style


00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.919
All we care about is talking


00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:51.920
Talking only me and you


00:04:52.920 --> 00:04:55.920
And we don't care about the young folks


00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.599
Talking about the young style


00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:02.479
And we don't care about the old folks


00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:05.480
Talking about the old style too


00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:09.240
And we don't care about our own faults


00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:12.719
Talking about our own style


00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.720
All we care about is talking


00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:18.800
Talking only me and you


00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:21.519
Talking only me and you


00:05:29.320 --> 00:05:30.919
Dear David Bowie,


00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:33.920
sometimes it seems like things
actually work out.


00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.840
English, Irene. English. There is
no such thing as conversational Elvish.


00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:49.560
Sorry, Dewey.


00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.639
It's what they call you, isn't it?


00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:54.959
No.


00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.960
It was at your last school.
Or do you prefer "Junior"?


00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.519
Do you know your buddy,
his full name is Will Burton, Jr.?


00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:01.999
Did you know that I don't care?


00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.759
Well, he told you
his dad was famous, right?


00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:06.599
Or infamous, right, Dewey?
I mean, you still close to the old man?


00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:08.319
You probably don't get to talk to him
much anymore, do you?


00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.320
-I don't know what you're talking about.
-Well, I think you do, Dewey.


00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:15.080
I think you do, Dewey.


00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:24.240
Okay, that was surreal. Are you okay?


00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.040
I don't... I got... I gotta...


00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.959
What are you doing?


00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.960
You didn't answer my texts,
and you left me alone with the monsters.


00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.479
Sorry, I'm sick.


00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:48.480
My spidey-sense tells me you're lying.


00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:52.159
I'm thinking about changing schools.


00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.160
No way, my little friend. I'm not facing
the Neanderthals without you.


00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.440
Besides, if you change schools,
then you can't gain access to this.


00:07:01.720 --> 00:07:04.239
-What's that?
-Something private.


00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:07.240
Something I would only show
the manager of my band.


00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:10.639
Or my best friend.


00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:13.640
Scooch.


00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:17.000
Okay. You said we needed one song
that says who we are.


00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.360
Well, these say who I am.


00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:25.680
Little brothers.


00:07:25.960 --> 00:07:28.960
Little brothers again.


00:07:30.520 --> 00:07:32.519
-For your dad?
-No.


00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:34.999
Not for him, exactly.


00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.239
Inspired by him, I guess.
You know, things he said to me.


00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:40.240
But it's not just about my dad anymore.
That'd be, hello, weird.


00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:43.599
It's about everything.


00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:45.839
Wow, that's articulate.


00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:47.119
You know, there's other stuff in here, too.


00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:50.120
-I'm not saying any of it's good...
-Thanks.


00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:53.480
Hey. By accepting this, it means that there
will be no more talk of changing schools.


00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:59.120
Agreed?


00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:02.719
-Man, I'm good.
-Charlotte!


00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:05.319
-Charlotte! My mom is in the...
-I knew you were ticklish.


00:08:05.320 --> 00:08:08.320
You are so ticklish, I knew it.


00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:12.400
Somebody wanna tell me
what's going on in here?


00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:17.359
Get off his bed.


00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.479
Wait. You don't think...


00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.959
I saw you kiss him in the car.


00:08:22.960 --> 00:08:25.079
Well, that was
for educational purposes only.


00:08:25.080 --> 00:08:26.159
I wanna die.


00:08:26.160 --> 00:08:28.599
Did you hear that? He wants to die.
He needs help, Karen.


00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:30.719
Then I'll help him. I'm his mom.


00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:32.799
But I am wise in the ways of Will.


00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.800
I'm actually here, you know. These covers
don't literally make me disappear.


00:08:37.240 --> 00:08:39.719
You know what I think?
I think you're full of it, Charlotte.


00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.119
And when I think someone's full of it,
I don't trust them.


00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:44.119
Mom, will you stop interfering?


00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.959
Sorry, I'm not your friend,
I'm your mother. That's my job.


00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.960
No, Mom, you're supposed to give me
a little breathing room so I can have a life,


00:08:51.240 --> 00:08:53.599
instead of just saying that's what you want.


00:08:53.600 --> 00:08:56.319
-He's got a point, Karen.
-And you, I'm not a manager.


00:08:56.320 --> 00:08:59.320
I don't take on the biggest band
in school and change destiny. I can't.


00:09:01.840 --> 00:09:04.840
Will you both just please leave me alone?


00:09:09.240 --> 00:09:12.240
Get out.


00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.000
-Somebody called me Dewey today.
-What? How?


00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:28.400
-He must've found out about Dad.
-I hate them all.


00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:30.759
-Me too.
-You, however, I love.


00:09:30.760 --> 00:09:33.760
Yeah, but you married Dad.
We can't really trust your taste.


00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:38.040
I was 19. And he was a drummer.


00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:41.720
And overnight it made my mother
finally take me seriously,


00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.479
which is really all I wanted.


00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:44.559
-Mom?
-I... What?


00:09:44.560 --> 00:09:47.560
You're doing that thing
where you talk to me like I'm Oprah.


00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:50.640
I'll tell you this, though.
I'd marry him all over again to get you.


00:09:56.920 --> 00:09:59.920
I promise you're going to get
everything you deserve out of life.


00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:03.920
And a little bit of the next guy's.


00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.519
I'll never be


00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:19.520
A knight in armor with a sword in hand


00:10:21.640 --> 00:10:24.640
Ora kamikaze fighter


00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.439
Don't count on me


00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:31.440
To storm the barricades and take a stand


00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:37.240
Or hold my ground


00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:41.080
You'll never see any scars or wounds


00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:45.679
I don't walk on coals


00:10:45.680 --> 00:10:48.680
I won't walk on water


00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:52.439
I am no prince


00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:55.239
I am no saint


00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:58.240
I am not anyone's wildest dream


00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:03.680
But I will stand behind


00:11:04.560 --> 00:11:07.560
And be someone to fall back on


00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:19.880
That's the song.


00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.799
Some comedy


00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:32.639
You're bruised and beaten down


00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:35.640
And I am the one who's looking for a favor


00:11:37.680 --> 00:11:40.039
Still, honestly


00:11:40.040 --> 00:11:43.040
You don't believe me
But the things I have


00:11:43.680 --> 00:11:46.680
Are the things you need


00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:50.120
You look at me like I don't make sense


00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:53.920
Like a waste of time
Like it serves no purpose


00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:59.200
I am no prince
I am no saint


00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:03.880
And if that's what you believe you need


00:12:05.560 --> 00:12:08.560
You're wrong
You don't need much


00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:11.920
You need someone to fall back on


00:12:14.680 --> 00:12:17.680
And I'll be that
I'll take your side


00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.200
If I'm the only one


00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:25.520
I'm used to that


00:12:26.200 --> 00:12:28.479
I've been alone


00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:31.480
I'd rather be


00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:35.599
The half of us


00:12:35.600 --> 00:12:37.799
The least of you


00:12:37.800 --> 00:12:40.800
The best of me


00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:44.719
And I will be


00:12:44.720 --> 00:12:47.720
I'll be your prince
I'll be your saint


00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:52.280
I will go crashing through fences
in your name


00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:57.319
I will, I swear


00:12:57.320 --> 00:13:00.320
I'll be someone to fall back on


00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:04.680
I'll be the one who waits


00:13:05.360 --> 00:13:08.360
And for as long as you let me


00:13:09.120 --> 00:13:12.120
I will be the one you need


00:13:13.600 --> 00:13:16.600
I'll be someone to fall back on


00:13:30.240 --> 00:13:33.240
Someone to fall back on


00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:43.720
One to fall back on


00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:57.320
Dear David Bowie,


00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:01.120
just when it looked like things
might be okay,


00:14:02.160 --> 00:14:03.479
disaster struck.


00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:06.119
What's going on? Where is everybody?


00:14:06.120 --> 00:14:09.120
-Art class is cancelled today.
-Why? What happened?


00:14:11.280 --> 00:14:14.280
Charlotte's father passed away.


00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.479
I assumed you knew.


00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:21.480
No.


00:14:32.920 --> 00:14:35.920
This was a mistake. We shouldn't be here.


00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:39.440
She didn't return any of my calls.


00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:43.839
-You going to be okay?
-Yeah.


00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:46.479
Okay.


00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:49.480
Go, she's your friend. She needs you.


00:14:58.400 --> 00:15:01.400
- Boys...
- I got them.


00:15:10.840 --> 00:15:13.840
Charlotte?


00:15:15.160 --> 00:15:18.160
I'm sorry.


00:15:20.680 --> 00:15:22.119
I called.


00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:25.120
I don't know if you got any of my messages.


00:15:27.040 --> 00:15:30.040
Yeah, I got them. Thanks.


00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:34.399
I wish you would've called me back.


00:15:34.400 --> 00:15:35.839
Why?


00:15:35.840 --> 00:15:37.279
"Why?"


00:15:37.280 --> 00:15:39.919
I don't know. I mean, you told Ben.


00:15:39.920 --> 00:15:42.559
So?


00:15:42.560 --> 00:15:43.679
Is anything wrong?


00:15:43.680 --> 00:15:45.159
Yeah.


00:15:45.160 --> 00:15:46.399
Yeah, my dad died.


00:15:46.400 --> 00:15:47.959
No, I know.


00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.960
I wish I could've met him.
I'm sure he was a great man.


00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:56.760
He was.


00:15:57.400 --> 00:16:00.400
I got to do this.


00:16:01.920 --> 00:16:04.239
Charlotte.


00:16:04.240 --> 00:16:07.240
Charlotte.


00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:09.439
-What do you want, Will?
-What do I want?


00:16:09.440 --> 00:16:11.279
I just want you to know that I'm here
for you.


00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.039
Okay, got it. What else?


00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:15.959
And not to worry about the daycare.
I can handle that until you come back.


00:16:15.960 --> 00:16:17.039
That's it.


00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:18.039
Listen, I'm sorry, okay.


00:16:18.040 --> 00:16:20.439
It's just a lot to deal with right now,
and I sort of want to be alone.


00:16:20.440 --> 00:16:21.679
Okay. I get it, yeah.


00:16:21.680 --> 00:16:22.839
And look, about the band...


00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:25.840
Don't even worry about the band, okay?
We'll use Phil's Song for Bandslam.


00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:30.119
Or not. We don't have to use Phil's Song.
We can find another song, or...


00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:33.120
Hey, go ahead. Knock yourselves out.


00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:39.920
I mean, it's a beautiful song, Charlotte.


00:16:40.160 --> 00:16:42.519
It would make your dad proud.
It would be like he's there.


00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:45.439
Stop! Please, just stop!


00:16:45.440 --> 00:16:47.319
There is no us, Will. I'm not in the band.


00:16:47.320 --> 00:16:50.320
What? No, no, no.
Okay, we'll find another song...


00:16:50.600 --> 00:16:53.439
It's not about the song. I quit. I just quit.


00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:54.839
-Why?
-I don't do "why"!


00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:57.840
No, you have to. You just have to!


00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:07.520
Please.


00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:14.999
You really want to know why?


00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:18.000
Last summer, when my dad got sick,


00:17:19.520 --> 00:17:22.520
I promised God, the universe,


00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:27.199
anyone who'd listen,


00:17:27.200 --> 00:17:29.399
that I'd be different.


00:17:29.400 --> 00:17:32.400
Better. Nicer.


00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:36.840
My dad hated the way I acted
when I was with Ben.


00:17:37.440 --> 00:17:40.440
The way I treated kids who weren't popular.


00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:43.319
So, I changed.


00:17:43.320 --> 00:17:46.320
I started volunteering with the monsters.
I left my friends. I left my band.


00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:51.480
I left everything that set me apart
from people like...


00:17:53.000 --> 00:17:56.000
Me.


00:17:57.800 --> 00:18:00.800
People like me.


00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:05.119
So we were just this


00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:07.959
experiment to try and make your dad okay?


00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:09.839
No, I know how crazy this must sound...


00:18:09.840 --> 00:18:12.799
Honestly, Charlotte,
the thing that never made sense


00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:15.800
was you being my friend in the first place.


00:18:18.720 --> 00:18:21.720
Hey!
While you're up there on your high horse,


00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:25.000
ask yourself who are you
to judge me about lying?


00:18:25.360 --> 00:18:28.360
Dewey!


00:18:33.160 --> 00:18:35.479
That stands for DWI, right?


00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:38.480
Driving while intoxicated?


00:18:39.560 --> 00:18:42.560
I don't know what's worse.


00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:46.720
Losing a father you love so much
you change your whole life for him,


00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:55.080
or having a father you're so ashamed of,
you make up a whole life for him.


00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:33.879
Can I have some beef jerky?


00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:36.880
Is he kidding?


00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:41.640
You warned me about her.


00:19:41.720 --> 00:19:43.439
I didn't listen.


00:19:43.440 --> 00:19:46.440
She can't help it.
It's how girls like that are hardwired.


00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:52.520
How are we hardwired?


00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:55.720
I mean, sure, right now, I am just a kid.


00:19:57.600 --> 00:20:00.600
Whatever.


00:20:01.560 --> 00:20:04.439
What's going to change?


00:20:04.440 --> 00:20:06.639
Nothing.


00:20:06.640 --> 00:20:09.239
I'm just going to be


00:20:09.240 --> 00:20:12.240
unhappy,


00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:14.999
alone,


00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:18.000
scared of, like, everything.


00:20:21.800 --> 00:20:24.800
You're not alone, Will.


00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:35.120
Experiment? We were just her experiment?


00:20:35.960 --> 00:20:37.839
I keep thinking...


00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:39.159
What?


00:20:39.160 --> 00:20:42.160
Well, if you were just part of
Charlotte's experiment this whole time,


00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:45.759
